1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:05,190
What if I told you that one week changed
the Agnipath scheme,

2
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:09,910
your Deepavali crackers, the rights of
every arrested person,

3
00:00:10,170 --> 00:00:13,020
and even the price of cancer medicines?

4
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:15,590
All of this happened in just one week.

5
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:17,080
I am Mounika,

6
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:21,520
and today we will decode the 15 strongest
stories of November's first week,

7
00:00:21,570 --> 00:00:26,980
with the static fact behind each one and
the exact trap UPSC can set.

8
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:28,540
Let's begin our journey.

9
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:32,450
Here is our map for today: five stories on
law and welfare,

10
00:00:32,670 --> 00:00:36,461
four on the economy, three on defence, one
from the world,

11
00:00:36,650 --> 00:00:41,571
and two important days, plus one alert for
Telugu aspirants at the end.

12
00:00:41,912 --> 00:00:48,262
Let us start with the story every defence
aspirant is searching for:

13
00:00:48,302 --> 00:00:51,012
has the Agnipath scheme been scrapped?

14
00:00:51,639 --> 00:00:54,144
Agnipath began in June 2022,

15
00:00:54,356 --> 00:01:01,134
recruiting young people between 17 and a
half and 21 years of age as Agniveers for

16
00:01:01,174 --> 00:01:07,886
four years, and only about one in four
were to stay on as regular soldiers.

17
00:01:07,986 --> 00:01:11,586
This week the Union Cabinet approved a big
change:

18
00:01:11,626 --> 00:01:16,193
about three in four Agniveers will get two
more years of service,

19
00:01:16,233 --> 00:01:19,961
with higher pay and a bigger Seva Nidhi
exit package,

20
00:01:20,001 --> 00:01:25,196
and a pathway to regular enrolment for
those who are willing and meet the

21
00:01:25,236 --> 00:01:26,656
selection criteria.

22
00:01:26,954 --> 00:01:31,794
Prelims trap: the scheme has not been
scrapped; it has been modified,

23
00:01:32,454 --> 00:01:36,589
and entry is still through the four-year
Agniveer route.

24
00:01:36,629 --> 00:01:40,484
Remember this. And for Mains, think
of the trade-off:

25
00:01:40,677 --> 00:01:47,089
a younger army on one side, and experience
and training costs on the other.

26
00:01:47,204 --> 00:01:50,909
Now, your first question of the day.

27
00:01:50,949 --> 00:01:56,745
Read both statements and decide: which of
them is correct?

28
00:02:03,930 --> 00:02:04,960
The answer is A,

29
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,150
statement 1 only. The scheme was modified,
not scrapped,

30
00:02:10,370 --> 00:02:14,200
so entry is still through the four-year
Agniveer route.

31
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,670
Give yourself your first tick!

32
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:21,290
And with Deepavali here, our second story
asks:

33
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:24,290
can the Supreme Court decide how you
celebrate a festival?

34
00:02:24,696 --> 00:02:25,836
On November second,

35
00:02:25,876 --> 00:02:30,944
the Supreme Court allowed only certified
green crackers in Delhi and the National

36
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:34,529
Capital Region, on the seventh and eighth,

37
00:02:34,569 --> 00:02:39,451
from six to seven in the morning and eight
to 10 at night,

38
00:02:39,491 --> 00:02:42,666
and never within 300 metres of hospitals,

39
00:02:43,115 --> 00:02:45,452
schools and silence zones.

40
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,755
Why can a court do this?

41
00:02:47,795 --> 00:02:54,003
Because the freedom of religion under
Article 25 is subject to public health,

42
00:02:54,043 --> 00:02:59,070
and the right to life under Article 21
includes clean air.

43
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:02,690
The Court said pollution defeats the very
purpose of the festival.

44
00:03:02,730 --> 00:03:08,480
Now the trap. Green crackers were designed
by the National Environmental Engineering

45
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:10,110
Research Institute in Nagpur,

46
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,490
and they contain no barium nitrate.

47
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:15,570
But the institute only designs the
formula;

48
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:18,630
the Petroleum and Explosives Safety
Organisation,

49
00:03:19,370 --> 00:03:26,570
under the Commerce Ministry, licenses the
makers under the Explosives Act of 102.

50
00:03:27,212 --> 00:03:36,242
Your turn. How many of these three pairs
are correctly matched?

51
00:03:41,683 --> 00:03:45,893
The answer is B, only two.

52
00:03:45,933 --> 00:03:50,923
The explosives safety organisation works
under the Commerce Ministry,

53
00:03:51,243 --> 00:03:52,841
not the Environment Ministry.

54
00:03:52,881 --> 00:03:57,691
Story three is very close to home for us
in the Telugu states:

55
00:03:57,791 --> 00:04:01,781
can having a third child stop you from
contesting a panchayat election?

56
00:04:02,327 --> 00:04:08,037
This week the Supreme Court said laws that
disqualify people with more than two

57
00:04:08,077 --> 00:04:11,087
children from panchayat elections have
lost relevance,

58
00:04:11,537 --> 00:04:17,117
and sent its 2003 Javed judgment, which
upheld such a law in Haryana,

59
00:04:17,587 --> 00:04:19,227
to a larger bench.

60
00:04:19,307 --> 00:04:20,927
The reason is data:

61
00:04:21,157 --> 00:04:27,307
India's total fertility rate has fallen
from about three to 1.9,

62
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:30,807
below the replacement level of 2.1.

63
00:04:30,847 --> 00:04:32,767
And who makes these rules?

64
00:04:32,957 --> 00:04:38,967
Article 243F lets each state's law decide
panchayat disqualifications,

65
00:04:39,917 --> 00:04:45,757
while the Court now asks whether punishing
family size hurts reproductive choice

66
00:04:45,797 --> 00:04:46,612
under Article 21.

67
00:04:46,652 --> 00:04:48,892
Telugu states lens:

68
00:04:49,052 --> 00:04:54,552
Andhra Pradesh had this rule since 1994
and scrapped it in 2024,

69
00:04:54,942 --> 00:04:59,092
and Telangana removed it for rural bodies
in 2026.

70
00:04:59,372 --> 00:05:03,092
But remember the trap: the Supreme Court
has not struck the rule down;

71
00:05:03,392 --> 00:05:06,292
it only referred the question to a larger
bench.

72
00:05:06,971 --> 00:05:10,691
Now a Statement-one, Statement-two
question,

73
00:05:10,761 --> 00:05:12,201
the format UPSC loves.

74
00:05:12,241 --> 00:05:17,601
Both may be true, so decide: does the
second explain the first?

75
00:05:22,626 --> 00:05:26,393
The answer is B.

76
00:05:26,563 --> 00:05:28,013
Both statements are correct,

77
00:05:28,053 --> 00:05:32,543
but Article 243F does not explain the
reference;

78
00:05:32,843 --> 00:05:37,945
falling fertility and reproductive choice
do.

79
00:05:38,695 --> 00:05:41,805
Story four protects every one of us:

80
00:05:42,115 --> 00:05:46,781
when exactly does the twenty-four-hour
clock start after the police pick you up?

81
00:05:46,821 --> 00:05:48,718
Article 22, clause 2,

82
00:05:48,758 --> 00:05:54,667
says an arrested person must be produced
before the nearest magistrate within 24

83
00:05:54,807 --> 00:05:57,608
hours, leaving out only the travel time.

84
00:05:57,648 --> 00:05:59,487
In a drug case from Tripura,

85
00:05:59,527 --> 00:06:03,177
the police held four people for searches
and paperwork,

86
00:06:03,217 --> 00:06:05,634
and recorded the arrest much later.

87
00:06:05,674 --> 00:06:07,107
On November fifth,

88
00:06:07,147 --> 00:06:12,136
the Supreme Court said there is no
difference between detention and arrest

89
00:06:12,176 --> 00:06:16,665
here: the clock starts the moment your
liberty is curtailed,

90
00:06:16,705 --> 00:06:19,177
and it ordered the four released.

91
00:06:19,277 --> 00:06:23,868
It also overruled the Orissa, Kerala and
Madras High Courts,

92
00:06:23,908 --> 00:06:27,137
which had allowed such time to be left
out.

93
00:06:27,179 --> 00:06:30,859
Prelims trap: the 24 hours run from
detention,

94
00:06:31,229 --> 00:06:34,159
not from the time the arrest is written
down,

95
00:06:34,379 --> 00:06:37,919
and the only time excluded is the journey
to the magistrate.

96
00:06:38,419 --> 00:06:41,369
Also remember, Article 22, clause 3,

97
00:06:41,409 --> 00:06:48,719
says these safeguards do not apply to an
enemy alien or to a person held under

98
00:06:48,759 --> 00:06:49,899
preventive detention.

99
00:06:50,569 --> 00:06:56,159
Pause and answer: which one statement
about Article 22, clause 2, is correct?

100
00:07:02,765 --> 00:07:04,595
The answer is B.

101
00:07:04,675 --> 00:07:09,565
The clock starts at detention, and only
the journey time is excluded.

102
00:07:10,335 --> 00:07:14,615
Story five is about speedy justice for
women and children.

103
00:07:14,705 --> 00:07:20,209
The Cabinet extended the fast-track
special courts scheme till March 2031,

104
00:07:20,406 --> 00:07:24,194
with about 3,788 crore rupees,

105
00:07:24,234 --> 00:07:28,819
and raised the number of courts from 779
to 850.

106
00:07:29,019 --> 00:07:33,949
These courts hear rape cases and cases
under the Protection of Children from

107
00:07:33,989 --> 00:07:37,289
Sexual Offences Act. The scheme began in
2019,

108
00:07:37,449 --> 00:07:40,769
after the Criminal Law Amendment Act of
2018.

109
00:07:40,809 --> 00:07:46,019
Prelims trap: it is a centrally sponsored
scheme, so the states share the cost,

110
00:07:46,059 --> 00:07:49,709
and the Centre's part comes from the
Nirbhaya Fund.

111
00:07:50,143 --> 00:07:52,183
Three statements on fast-track courts.

112
00:07:52,223 --> 00:07:54,523
How many of them are correct?

113
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:03,420
The answer is A, only one.

114
00:08:03,873 --> 00:08:07,457
The courts go up from 779 to 850,

115
00:08:07,497 --> 00:08:11,893
and they come from a centrally sponsored
scheme, not a separate Act.

116
00:08:12,775 --> 00:08:14,805
Five stories done, 10 to go.

117
00:08:14,845 --> 00:08:15,895
If you have come this far,

118
00:08:15,935 --> 00:08:20,495
you are a serious aspirant! Now let us move
from rights and courts to villages,

119
00:08:20,535 --> 00:08:21,975
power and money.

120
00:08:22,325 --> 00:08:25,035
Story six touches every village:

121
00:08:25,215 --> 00:08:29,610
what can a worker do if the work or the
wages never come?

122
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:30,845
From July first,

123
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:35,717
the Viksit Bharat Guarantee for Rozgar and
Ajeevika Mission, Gramin,

124
00:08:35,757 --> 00:08:40,384
Act replaced the Mahatma Gandhi National
Rural Employment Guarantee Act,

125
00:08:40,424 --> 00:08:44,761
and raised the guarantee from 100 to 125
days of work.

126
00:08:44,801 --> 00:08:49,174
This week the Rural Development Ministry
notified its grievance rules:

127
00:08:49,214 --> 00:08:54,186
a complaint can be filed in person, by
post, online or on a helpline,

128
00:08:54,226 --> 00:09:00,732
and it must be enquired into within seven
working days and solved within 15,

129
00:09:01,142 --> 00:09:04,093
at Gram Panchayat, Block and District
level.

130
00:09:04,221 --> 00:09:07,711
Prelims trap: the Centre no longer pays
all the wages;

131
00:09:07,871 --> 00:09:11,891
the cost is now shared 60 to 40 with the
states,

132
00:09:11,931 --> 00:09:15,641
and 90 to 10 for Himalayan and
north-eastern states.

133
00:09:15,841 --> 00:09:16,981
Telugu states lens:

134
00:09:17,171 --> 00:09:21,351
united Andhra Pradesh pioneered social
audits of this programme,

135
00:09:21,671 --> 00:09:24,593
with its own audit society from 2009.

136
00:09:24,633 --> 00:09:28,493
Now the rural jobs law.

137
00:09:28,533 --> 00:09:30,235
How many of these three statements are

138
00:09:36,393 --> 00:09:35,896
correct?

139
00:09:35,936 --> 00:09:44,476
The answer is C, all three: 125 days, 60
to 40 sharing,

140
00:09:44,516 --> 00:09:46,856
and 15 days to resolve a complaint.

141
00:09:47,516 --> 00:09:54,006
Story seven answers a simple question:
what happens to solar power after sunset?

142
00:09:54,046 --> 00:10:01,596
The Cabinet approved 14,500 crore rupees
of viability gap funding to build 92

143
00:10:01,746 --> 00:10:06,316
gigawatt-hours of grid-scale storage: 60
from pumped storage,

144
00:10:06,476 --> 00:10:09,636
30 from batteries and two from new
technologies.

145
00:10:10,216 --> 00:10:15,146
Viability gap funding means the government
pays part of the cost,

146
00:10:15,236 --> 00:10:20,036
so that a project which is useful but not
yet profitable becomes viable.

147
00:10:20,376 --> 00:10:23,976
Pumped storage is like a giant water
battery:

148
00:10:24,386 --> 00:10:27,226
you pump water uphill when power is cheap,

149
00:10:27,266 --> 00:10:30,956
and let it fall through turbines when it
is needed.

150
00:10:31,376 --> 00:10:35,560
Prelims trap: the biggest share here is
pumped storage, not batteries.

151
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:42,820
A quick one on storage: which part of the
92 gigawatt-hours is the largest?

152
00:10:49,701 --> 00:10:55,101
The answer is B, pumped storage, with 60
of the 92 gigawatt-hours.

153
00:10:56,619 --> 00:10:59,909
Story eight follows the battery inside
your phone:

154
00:11:00,119 --> 00:11:02,429
where does its lithium get processed?

155
00:11:02,530 --> 00:11:07,069
Lithium and nickel are critical minerals
for batteries and electric vehicles,

156
00:11:07,109 --> 00:11:10,599
but processing them is concentrated in a
few countries.

157
00:11:10,839 --> 00:11:17,989
So the Cabinet approved a 2,814 crore
rupee scheme that pays 30% of the capital

158
00:11:18,039 --> 00:11:23,018
cost of four processing plants in India,
two for lithium and two for nickel,

159
00:11:23,058 --> 00:11:27,903
over five years. Notice the chain: our
storage story needs batteries,

160
00:11:27,993 --> 00:11:29,544
and batteries need processed minerals.

161
00:11:29,584 --> 00:11:32,954
Prelims trap: this scheme is about
processing,

162
00:11:33,244 --> 00:11:34,794
not mining or recycling.

163
00:11:34,994 --> 00:11:39,574
Recycling has its own 1,500 crore rupee
scheme from 2025.

164
00:11:40,274 --> 00:11:42,814
Another Statement-one, Statement-two
question.

165
00:11:42,854 --> 00:11:45,104
Does the second statement explain the
first?

166
00:11:51,694 --> 00:11:52,894
The answer is A.

167
00:11:53,714 --> 00:11:54,684
Both are correct,

168
00:11:54,724 --> 00:11:59,504
and the concentration of processing abroad
is exactly why the scheme was approved.

169
00:12:00,937 --> 00:12:04,607
Story nine is about the numbers behind
every policy:

170
00:12:05,197 --> 00:12:07,587
how does India count its shops and
factories?

171
00:12:07,929 --> 00:12:09,529
The Cabinet approved VISTAR,

172
00:12:09,569 --> 00:12:14,418
a scheme of about 4,371 crore rupees over
five years,

173
00:12:14,458 --> 00:12:19,059
to modernise India's statistical system
with digital tools and artificial

174
00:12:19,099 --> 00:12:24,469
intelligence. It will run 59 surveys and
the eighth Economic Census,

175
00:12:24,538 --> 00:12:29,099
which counts every non-farm establishment
and its workers.

176
00:12:29,139 --> 00:12:34,199
Prelims trap: the Economic Census is run
by the Ministry of Statistics and

177
00:12:34,239 --> 00:12:40,111
Programme Implementation, while the
Population Census is run by the Registrar

178
00:12:40,151 --> 00:12:44,062
General and Census Commissioner under the
Home Ministry.

179
00:12:44,162 --> 00:12:45,312
Now the census trap.

180
00:12:45,352 --> 00:12:48,192
How many of these three statements are
correct?

181
00:12:54,772 --> 00:12:56,802
The answer is C, all three.

182
00:12:56,842 --> 00:13:00,482
The Economic Census sits with the
Statistics Ministry,

183
00:13:00,522 --> 00:13:04,942
and the Population Census with the
Registrar General under the Home Ministry.

184
00:13:05,585 --> 00:13:10,235
Story 10: why was India still flying under
rules written in 1937?

185
00:13:10,275 --> 00:13:17,385
The Civil Aviation Ministry notified the
Bharatiya Vayuyan Niyam, 2026,

186
00:13:17,725 --> 00:13:23,015
which replace the colonial-era Aircraft
Rules of 1937 from January first,

187
00:13:23,055 --> 00:13:29,075
2027. They cover aircraft registration,
safety, licences and airports,

188
00:13:29,665 --> 00:13:34,395
and they let the government step in on air
fares in extraordinary situations.

189
00:13:34,905 --> 00:13:38,035
Prelims trap: the Niyam are the rules;

190
00:13:38,075 --> 00:13:43,195
the parent law is the Bharatiya Vayuyan
Adhiniyam of 2024,

191
00:13:43,425 --> 00:13:46,755
which replaced the Aircraft Act of 1934.

192
00:13:47,517 --> 00:13:50,467
Rules or Act? How many of these three
statements are correct?

193
00:13:54,419 --> 00:13:59,539
The answer is B, only two.

194
00:13:59,579 --> 00:14:03,719
The new rules actually let the government
step in on fares in extraordinary

195
00:14:04,189 --> 00:14:05,189
situations.

196
00:14:05,559 --> 00:14:09,249
10 done! Now let's look at defence
and the world.

197
00:14:09,919 --> 00:14:13,966
Story 11 is a missile with a dramatic
name: Pralay.

198
00:14:14,006 --> 00:14:15,379
On November fifth,

199
00:14:15,419 --> 00:14:20,271
the Defence Research and Development
Organisation flight-tested Pralay from

200
00:14:20,311 --> 00:14:24,164
Doctor A P J Abdul Kalam Island off
Odisha.

201
00:14:24,204 --> 00:14:30,109
Pralay is a quasi-ballistic missile, which
means it can change its path in flight,

202
00:14:30,539 --> 00:14:32,606
so it is harder to intercept.

203
00:14:32,646 --> 00:14:35,937
Prelims trap: Agni and Prithvi are
ballistic missiles,

204
00:14:35,977 --> 00:14:39,892
while BrahMos is a cruise missile built
with Russia,

205
00:14:39,932 --> 00:14:41,557
so do not mix up the families.

206
00:14:41,597 --> 00:14:46,687
Missile families: how many of these four
pairs are correctly matched?

207
00:14:52,413 --> 00:14:55,471
The answer is C, only three.

208
00:14:55,511 --> 00:15:00,240
Prithvi is a ballistic missile, not a
cruise missile.

209
00:15:00,926 --> 00:15:05,751
From land to sea: our 12th story is
Exercise Malabar.

210
00:15:05,791 --> 00:15:11,921
Malabar 2026 is being held off Honshu in
Japan from the fifth to the 12th of

211
00:15:11,961 --> 00:15:17,041
November, with the navies of India, the
United States, Japan and Australia,

212
00:15:17,491 --> 00:15:20,551
the same four countries that form the
Quad.

213
00:15:20,811 --> 00:15:24,381
India has sent the frigate Indian Naval
Ship Sahyadri.

214
00:15:24,669 --> 00:15:30,523
Prelims trap: Malabar began in 1992 as a
two-nation exercise between India and the

215
00:15:30,563 --> 00:15:34,214
United States; Japan became a permanent
member in 2015,

216
00:15:34,254 --> 00:15:36,197
and Australia rejoined in 2020.

217
00:15:36,237 --> 00:15:40,817
Arrange these three Malabar milestones in
the correct order.

218
00:15:47,407 --> 00:15:50,187
The answer is A: three, one,

219
00:15:50,227 --> 00:15:54,007
two. 1992, then 2015, then 2020.

220
00:15:54,691 --> 00:15:58,808
Story 13 is the biggest election story of
the week, from the United States.

221
00:15:58,848 --> 00:16:00,181
In America's midterm elections,

222
00:16:00,221 --> 00:16:03,589
the Democrats won control of the House of
Representatives,

223
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:07,646
and reports say they may control the
Senate too,

224
00:16:07,756 --> 00:16:09,856
though the final count is still pending.

225
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:15,366
Remember the structure: the House has 435
members elected every two years,

226
00:16:15,406 --> 00:16:19,150
while the Senate has 100 members with
six-year terms,

227
00:16:19,190 --> 00:16:23,197
and about a third face election every two
years.

228
00:16:23,237 --> 00:16:28,411
They are called midterms because they fall
halfway through the President's four-year

229
00:16:28,571 --> 00:16:29,131
term.

230
00:16:29,171 --> 00:16:30,451
Now connect it to India,

231
00:16:30,491 --> 00:16:32,931
because this is a favourite trap.

232
00:16:32,971 --> 00:16:35,591
Our Rajya Sabha works like the American
Senate:

233
00:16:35,891 --> 00:16:40,511
members serve six years and about 4th
retire every two years,

234
00:16:40,551 --> 00:16:44,741
so the Rajya Sabha is a permanent house
that is never dissolved.

235
00:16:44,981 --> 00:16:48,931
The Lok Sabha, like the House of
Representatives, is directly elected,

236
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:50,125
but for five years, not two.

237
00:16:50,165 --> 00:16:51,575
Now the India bridge.

238
00:16:51,615 --> 00:16:55,515
How many of these three statements are
correct?

239
00:16:59,190 --> 00:17:04,300
The answer is B, only two.

240
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:07,340
The Rajya Sabha is a permanent house and
is never dissolved.

241
00:17:08,041 --> 00:17:09,441
Now two important days.

242
00:17:09,481 --> 00:17:10,083
Story 14 was on November fifth.

243
00:17:10,123 --> 00:17:14,493
The International Day against Violence and
Bullying at School,

244
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:18,983
including Cyberbullying, is held on the
first Thursday of November.

245
00:17:19,453 --> 00:17:22,853
It was declared by the member states of
the United Nations Educational,

246
00:17:22,963 --> 00:17:28,343
Scientific and Cultural Organization in
2019 and first observed in 2020,

247
00:17:29,303 --> 00:17:33,513
and one in three students worldwide has
been bullied in the past month.

248
00:17:34,783 --> 00:17:38,813
Prelims trap: India's National Commission
for Protection of Child Rights is a

249
00:17:38,853 --> 00:17:43,275
statutory body under a 2005 Act, not a
constitutional one.

250
00:17:43,315 --> 00:17:49,715
Which one of these correctly describes the
National Commission for Protection of

251
00:17:49,755 --> 00:17:50,675
Child Rights?

252
00:17:57,262 --> 00:18:02,292
The answer is B, a statutory body under
the 2005 Act.

253
00:18:02,695 --> 00:18:07,085
And story 15: November seventh is National
Cancer Awareness Day,

254
00:18:07,125 --> 00:18:10,365
and this year it comes with good news on
medicine prices.

255
00:18:10,445 --> 00:18:13,632
The day falls on Marie Curie's birthday,

256
00:18:13,679 --> 00:18:16,427
and India has marked it since 2014.

257
00:18:16,467 --> 00:18:17,879
From November ninth,

258
00:18:17,919 --> 00:18:23,113
the National Pharmaceutical Pricing
Authority caps the trade margin on 137

259
00:18:23,389 --> 00:18:26,690
anti-cancer medicines at 30%,

260
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:32,084
using paragraph 19 of the Drugs Prices
Control Order of 2013,

261
00:18:32,124 --> 00:18:37,122
so some prices may fall by up to 70%.

262
00:18:37,321 --> 00:18:41,691
Two traps here. Marie Curie won two Nobel
Prizes in two different sciences,

263
00:18:41,881 --> 00:18:45,471
Physics in 19 oh three and Chemistry in
1911.

264
00:18:45,621 --> 00:18:49,571
And the pricing authority sits under the
Department of Pharmaceuticals in the

265
00:18:49,611 --> 00:18:54,091
Chemicals and Fertilizers Ministry, not
under the Health Ministry.

266
00:18:54,681 --> 00:18:55,971
The last topic question.

267
00:18:56,161 --> 00:18:58,851
How many of these four statements are
correct?

268
00:19:02,055 --> 00:19:07,675
The answer is C, only three.

269
00:19:07,715 --> 00:19:10,905
The pricing authority works under the
Department of Pharmaceuticals,

270
00:19:11,205 --> 00:19:12,535
not the Health Ministry.

271
00:19:13,868 --> 00:19:16,158
One alert for Telugu aspirants:

272
00:19:16,198 --> 00:19:20,508
Andhra Pradesh has announced its District
Selection Committee teacher recruitment

273
00:19:20,548 --> 00:19:23,508
for about 2,721 posts,

274
00:19:23,548 --> 00:19:26,158
with applications reported from November
11th.

275
00:19:26,388 --> 00:19:28,768
Please check the official website for
exact details.

276
00:19:29,278 --> 00:19:32,508
And for Mains, here is this week's one
writing question:

277
00:19:32,558 --> 00:19:38,748
is the protection of Article 22 real only
if the twenty-four-hour clock runs from

278
00:19:38,788 --> 00:19:40,873
the moment liberty is curtailed?

279
00:19:40,913 --> 00:19:44,038
Write 150 words in seven minutes,

280
00:19:44,078 --> 00:19:46,009
and write your answer in the comments.

281
00:19:46,049 --> 00:19:49,173
All 15 practice MCQs, with answers,

282
00:19:49,213 --> 00:19:53,828
are in the practice sheet linked in the
description.

283
00:19:54,518 --> 00:19:56,728
That was November's first week: 15
stories,

284
00:19:56,768 --> 00:20:01,475
15 traps. If this helped, share it with
one friend who is preparing with you,

285
00:20:01,515 --> 00:20:03,763
and subscribe for every Sunday's class.

286
00:20:03,803 --> 00:20:05,256
Happy Deepavali to everyone,
let's celebrate it green!

